{"title":"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Solution_1_with_more_reasoning)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Solution 1 with more reasoning)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_of_Logic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power of Logic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a positive real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> not equal to either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740a46a9368bf89084baff7d243944accc68cd0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/218c6b3e76211f744168e77b8ad9822ccce27d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b2d644c3c35696b97f664a77cacdd39b6995abf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{20x} (22x)=\\log_{2x} (202x).\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" />The value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b28c7f23bd77941b917954e733ce4539cf21b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{20x} (22x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220099aa8d9b0a42e94d0151765f7b2329454e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} (\\tfrac{m}{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"69\" height=\"22\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228ef48aeb485fc8e0d12e6d648e1bb9a4428a19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{20x} (22x) = \\log_{2x} (202x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />, what we are looking for. Then, by the definition of the logarithm,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb53f40f70a821a1ce25f078915aabb87e1b1d37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases}  (20x)^{a} &amp;= 22x \\\\ (2x)^{a} &amp;= 202x.  \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"53\" />\nDividing the first equation by the second equation gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca1f9b8edabddd7849b8f3c7ea9e3a6e229612f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^a = \\frac{11}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />, so by the definition of logs, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01a6c6f110e84a5a5ce3224e6cf2cd0b107c4e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\log_{10} \\frac{11}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />. This is what the problem asked for, so the fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1391fabeaa53458a3e33cc673464fd5f99eb5e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83ab9a321743b1da96e43c360e68e5f32fb3c1df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ihatemath123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We could assume a variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> which equals to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b28c7f23bd77941b917954e733ce4539cf21b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{20x} (22x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439846a43dec86bdc949ed212393a07119fd89b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2x} (202x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>So that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7b51be3f802a7ff7786cb18548e0167f63e9e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20x)^v=22x \\textcircled{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f5ae81e37490a4f57cadbd7ce4df1d8b8f7cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x)^v=202x \\textcircled{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b86f697d2110423d055cd0d6a8245af8b662987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textcircled{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> as: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4307898a887b4258262d011c3d10d2ee9c719a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20x)^v=(2x \\cdot 10)^v=(2x)^v \\cdot \\left(10^v\\right)=22x \\textcircled{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e08c314cfb1d3164996bef4f4fa9c71f255596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textcircled{{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e615216bca8604528e1313877f58ff8f7ea34b5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textcircled{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fc6d9040bcff261cea89c080fb4b596683808e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$202x \\cdot (10^v)=22x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/388edf31205afe0e8d79931d6f4d09560f24fc31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v=\\log_{10} \\left(\\frac{22x}{202x}\\right)= \\log_{10} \\left(\\frac{11}{101}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"266\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa04cc089ba32d487230dfab931a567dbfb2ff48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20cb622b2e4a754fc3cb2025097b7162b6c3db25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=101$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83ab9a321743b1da96e43c360e68e5f32fb3c1df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3481795c4a7dcbe179ed50a0cfde6c4999f8d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{20x} (22x) &amp; = \\frac{\\log_k 22x}{\\log_k 20x} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\log_k x + \\log_k 22}{\\log_k x + \\log_k 20} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"239\" height=\"90\" />\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f178d5ff0dff2847c5130717552d843aa227e38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{2x} (202x) &amp; = \\frac{\\log_k 202x}{\\log_k 2x} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\log_k x + \\log_k 202 }{\\log_k x + \\log_k 2} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"251\" height=\"90\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63a2dabd19722a5d517ece8a9f6854388e88bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{20x} (22x)=\\log_{2x} (202x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f076c9f18f8c7ad160a6201e1cc43e7bee135e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\frac{\\log_k x + \\log_k 22}{\\log_k x + \\log_k 20} = \\frac{\\log_k x + \\log_k 202 }{\\log_k x + \\log_k 2} . \\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>We denote this common value as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>By solving the equality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b8e0304b38068cc511522370ebbf63b7f9f77b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_k x + \\log_k 22}{\\log_k x + \\log_k 20} = \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"161\" height=\"44\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/4568d16bdb8c39c6243992f8a21bd77a78472a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_k x = \\frac{\\log_k 22 - \\lambda \\log_k 20}{\\lambda - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"217\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>By solving the equality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f759fe002cbc937e0d13cfb6aa48ded5eaa114dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_k x + \\log_k 202 }{\\log_k x + \\log_k 2} = \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"170\" height=\"44\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460a0abd32f700c8e917ec214e0dfaf38933611e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_k x = \\frac{\\log_k 202 - \\lambda \\log_k 2}{\\lambda - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"217\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>By equating these two equations, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a894a519d5ca0af34e6d018943d469a7c01ef0c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\frac{\\log_k 22 - \\lambda \\log_k 20}{\\lambda - 1} = \\frac{\\log_k 202 - \\lambda \\log_k 2}{\\lambda - 1} . \\]\" width=\"317\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc12b0511fa988f9c81b3ca838b60b61fef49ef2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{20x} (22x) &amp; = \\lambda \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\log_k 22 - \\log_k 202}{\\log_k 20 - \\log_k 2} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\log_k \\frac{11}{101}}{\\log_k 10} \\\\ &amp; = \\log_{10} \\frac{11}{101} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"251\" height=\"162\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/467c39c6e4ea2894cd692ff0f5a843c23f74da2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 101 = \\boxed{\\textbf{112}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"134\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Solution_1_with_more_reasoning.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Solution_1_with_more_reasoning)\">Solution 4 (Solution 1 with more reasoning)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Solution 1 with more reasoning)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the exponent such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab42f08203a3e5712d63ab9cddbca24ab5b8b8e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20x)^a = 22x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/70111457e3e8781eaf8b82c741582856514f5960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x)^a = 202x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />. Dividing, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc5feb6d0260a1ab5f0f01346375a1363c4a1e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\dfrac{(20x)^a}{(2x)^a} &amp;= \\dfrac{22x}{202x}. \\\\ \\left(\\dfrac{20x}{2x}\\right)^a &amp;= \\dfrac{22x}{202x}. \\\\ 10^a &amp;= \\dfrac{11}{101}. \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"132\" height=\"136\" />\nThus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e04654dad66d296e1b7d3bba8881130fae39d417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} \\left(\\dfrac{11}{101}\\right) = a = \\log_{20x} 22x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"235\" height=\"45\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2da96cfbde87b5b39033feb3b3908692a600fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 101 = \\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~A_MatheMagician\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the change of base rule, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/5876800840de061d23576a8028e8304f4bc69876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log 22x}{\\log 20x}=\\frac{\\log 202x}{\\log 2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437278a251d027072f1b3b1405626a20d1697261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log 22 +\\log x}{\\log 20 +\\log x}=\\frac{\\log 202 +\\log x}{\\log 2 +\\log x}=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"285\" height=\"43\" />. We also know that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b70c267eaaee847c6f04a63b9fcbe4a4aa072d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/b=c/d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />, then this also equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b75692c013503e1320bf360f786046efd8292080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a-c}{b-d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"46\" height=\"39\" />. We use this identity and find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/674f54ffe3a6bac42cc5be3696ca920cff860145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{\\log 202 -\\log 22}{\\log 2 -\\log 20}=-\\log\\frac{202}{22}=\\log\\frac{11}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"342\" height=\"43\" />. The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1ba5bfdd8d2efdef884861581c9938d447820e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11+101=\\boxed{112}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"137\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~MathIsFun286\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By change of base formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05847a60e198f5c092e27663ba028815f8eea80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log_{2x} 22x}{\\log_{2x} 20x} = \\frac{{\\log_{2x} 11} + 1}{{\\log_{2x} 10} + 1} = {\\log_{2x} 101} + 1\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa0bbcd79b317032bf9438dff0819f783c519fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{2x} 11 + 1 = (\\log_{2x} 10)(\\log_{2x} 101) + \\log_{2x} 10 + 1\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8df2a6eb561d593b1050ff52f475748d317525.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log_{2x} \\frac{11}{1010}}{\\log_{2x} 10} = \\log_{2x} 101\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/23095432798b3e7e1533bc21edb640c73fa5269e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10} {\\frac{11}{1010}} = \\log_{2x} 101\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a41f9a7a25afc47b0a781f6de6833085daab9b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10} {\\frac{11}{1010}} + 1 = \\log_{2x} 101 + 1 = \\log_{2x} 202x = \\log_{20x} {22x}\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"37\" />\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e5bea46b728c0e9899caae8d3896c92d3b136e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{20x} 22x = \\log_{10} \\left( \\frac{11}{1010} \\times 10 \\right) = \\log_{10} \\frac{11}{101}\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"43\" />\nThe requested answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2da96cfbde87b5b39033feb3b3908692a600fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 101 = \\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ adam_zheng\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qJyvyZN630\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qJyvyZN630</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_of_Logic\">Video Solution by Power of Logic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power of Logic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/m2Cm9r5_Jvs\">https://youtu.be/m2Cm9r5_Jvs</a>\n</p><p>~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II\" title=\"2022 AIME II\">2022 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2022\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Prec